        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right ankle inspection"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild diffuse swelling around the lateral malleolus with faint resolving bruising. Skin intact; no erythema or deformity."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right ankle tenderness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Tender over the ATFL and mildly over the CFL. Minimal tenderness directly over the tip/posterior edge of the lateral malleolus. No bony tenderness at the medial malleolus, base of the 5th metatarsal, or navicular. No tenderness at the syndesmosis or midfoot."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right ankle range of motion"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Dorsiflexion and plantar flexion mildly limited at end range by pain. Inversion reproduces lateral pain; eversion causes minimal symptoms."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
